!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = Neural progenitor cells
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Mus musculus
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 10090
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: WT
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = passages: 5-20
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = P0 brain-derived neurosphere cells (NPC) cultures were obtained from dissected telencephalons of four mice, plated in 25-ml flasks and cultured to expand their number in complete medium (2% (vol/vol) B27 in DMEM F12 with Glutamax), supplemented with 10 ng ml−1 EGF, 10 ng ml−1 of basic fibroblast growth factor (FGF) with 0.2% (vol/vol) heparin. Cells were passaged two times, every fourth day (by 0.25% trypsin treatment for 5 min, followed by block with 1 mg ml−1 trypsin inhibitor (Sigma T6522) for 5 min). Neurospheres were then dissociated and cells were seeded at 80,000 per ml in T150 flasks, and expanded by passaging every 4 days in complete medium with EGF, but not FGF and heparin, for 3–5 passages until they reached 1 × 109 in number. To confirm that these cells were telencephalic, we further verified expression of some critical telencephalic markers.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Library was created using SOLID Whole Transcriptome Analysis Kit (Life Technologies). Briefly, poly(A) selected RNA was treated with RNAse III. Fragmented RNA were hybridized and ligated with adaptors. This is followed by a reverse transcription. cDNA was purified and subjected to a size selection on a PAGE gel. Fraction 125-200bp was excised and purified. Amplification was performed using SOLiD PCR primers for 15 cycles.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Trizol RNA extraction
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were filtered to remove sequences such as ribosomal RNA, transfer RNA, mitochondrial RNA and repeat sequences, etc.
!Sample_data_processing = The strand-specific (NSC & NPC) reads were mapped on mouse reference genome mm9 with SOLiD whole transcriptome alignment pipeline and analysed by Bioscope (v1.0.1) analysis pipeline. A split-read mapping approach was also applied to map reads that spanned two exons. For strand-specific ESC reads, Tophat (v2.0.9) with Bowtie2 (v2.0.6) were used.
!Sample_data_processing = Uniquely mapped reads were used to calculate expression values obtained for all RefSeq genes.
!Sample_data_processing = Expression values were determined as RPKM for coding sequences.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: mm9
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: tab-delimited text files of RPKM values for ESC, NSC and NPC gene locus
